+# PlacementRules spec cleanup
+
+`PlacementRules.spec.luau` goes from 31 tests to 20. Every rule in the doc comment on
+`PlacementRules.validate` and `PlacementRules.snap` is still covered. `PlacementRules.luau` is
+unchanged.
+
+## The two failing tests
+
+- **"rejects a position that isn't a Vector3"** called `expect(ok):toBe(false)` with a colon. In
+  Jest Roblox, matchers are called with a dot. The colon passes the expectation object as the
+  first argument, so the test failed even though `validate` behaves correctly. Fixed, and the case
+  is now a row in the bad-arguments table.
+- **"doesn't mark the cell occupied"** asserted `expect(count).toBeFalsy()` with `count = 0`. In
+  Luau only `false` and `nil` are falsy, so `0` always failed the assertion. It now asserts
+  `next(occupied)` is nil after an accepted request.
+
+## Removed
+
+| Test(s) | Why |
+|---|---|
+| `snap` "snaps positions to cell centers" | Tautological: it worked out the expected value with the same formula as `snap`, so it could never disagree with it. |
+| `snap` rows (1,1,1) and (2,2,2) | The same case as the other rows inside a cell. Kept one row for each side of a cell edge, plus a negative row. |
+| `_isFinite` (3 tests) | Tested a private helper, so they broke on refactors that kept behavior. NaN and infinity are now checked through `validate`. |
+| "calls snap exactly once" | Checked an internal call count. Inlining or caching the snap would break it even though placement still worked. |
+| "accepts a $Name block" (5 rows, one per block type) | `validate` treats every block type the same way, so one accepted type covers the rule. Those rows also used a module-level `occupied` table that later tests wrote to, so their result depended on test order. |
+| "returns the snapped center" | Merged into the accept test, which now checks the center against a value worked out by hand instead of against `snap`'s output. |
+| "rejects placing twice in the same cell" | It passed only because an earlier test had left the cell occupied. Merged into the occupied test, which now builds its own table and uses a position that differs from the stored center but lies in the same cell. |
+| `BlockTypes` "has the right block types" | Repeated catalog values (colors, materials, transparency) field by field. It broke on every art tweak and checked no rule. It also belongs to a `BlockTypes` spec, not this one. |
+
+## Changed
+
+- Reason strings are no longer asserted. `validate` documents them as "a short reason for the
+  server log", so their wording isn't part of the contract. Each refusal test starts from one
+  request that passes every check (the accept test proves it) and breaks exactly one rule.
+- Expected heights, reach distances, and cell sizes come from `PlacementRules.MaxHeight`,
+  `PlacementRules.MaxReach`, and `BlockTypes.BlockSize`, not from literals. Tuning those values no
+  longer breaks the spec.
+- Every test builds its own `occupied` table, so no test depends on another.
+- The spec now uses `--!strict`, `const`, and string requires, following the project's Luau style
+  guide.
+
+## Added
+
+- **No character**: a nil `rootPosition` is rejected. This rule is documented but had no test.
+- **A non-string block type**: `validate` takes raw remote arguments and checks `typeof` before
+  looking up the name.
+- **An infinite position**: until now only NaN was tested through `validate`.
+- **A diagonal reach row**: a character within `MaxReach` on each axis but farther away in a
+  straight line is rejected. This pins the straight-line distance the doc describes.
+
+## Coverage map (documented rule → test)
+
+| Rule | Test |
+|---|---|
+| `snap` returns the center of the containing cell, with cells aligned to the origin | `snap` table (4 rows) |
+| The cell resting on the Baseplate has center Y = BlockSize / 2 | `snap` row "a point on a cell's lower edge", and the height row "the cell resting on the Baseplate" |
+| Known block type | accept test; bad-arguments rows "unknown block type" and "not a string" |
+| Position is a Vector3 with finite components | bad-arguments rows: not a Vector3, NaN, infinite |
+| Above the Baseplate, no higher than MaxHeight | height table (4 rows, both sides of each limit) |
+| Has a character | "rejects a player with no character" |
+| Within MaxReach, exactly MaxReach counts as in reach | reach table (3 rows) |
+| Cell not already occupied | "rejects any position in a cell that is already occupied" |
+| Returns true and the cell's center | accept test |
+| Never changes `occupied` | "leaves occupied unchanged when it accepts" |
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- The doc says the center must be "above the Baseplate (Y > 0)", but the code rejects only
+  `Y < 0`. A cell center always sits at an odd multiple of BlockSize / 2, so it can never be
+  exactly 0, and the two checks agree. No test row targets Y = 0.
+- The test "leaves occupied unchanged" covers only the accept path. The refusal paths return
+  before they reach `occupied`.
+- Specs couldn't be run here. `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene src`, and `stylua --check src` pass.
+  Run the spec in Studio, or let CI run it, before merging.
